      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogue%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up in 1888 as a railroad hub for the Union Pacific line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogue%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bogue’s first post office opened in September 1888, marking the start of its community services.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogue%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bogue High School closed in 1978 when the district unified, ending a local era of high school sports.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
